       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.** The usual adult range is 50\u2013200 mg/day, and 200 mg/day is the labeled maximum. At 1000 mg there's a real risk of serotonin syndrome, QTc prolongation and seizures. This looks like it may be a typo, maybe for **100 mg**.\n\nCould you tell me which you meant?\n\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg PO once daily.** I can enter this as soon as you confirm.\n2. **A different dose.** Just tell me the amount.\n3. **1000 mg is intended.** If so, please share the clinical reason. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy, since a dose this far above the maximum will likely need their review."
