     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter sertraline 1000 mg daily, even with your confirmation. There's no recognized indication for a dose that high. At 5 times the labeled maximum, the risks of serotonin toxicity, QTc prolongation and seizures are serious enough that I don't think I should place it without more context. I'm also wary because a 10-fold error (100 \u2192 1000 mg) is one of the most common serious ordering mistakes.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n1. **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 100 mg or up to the 200 mg maximum, PO once daily.\n2. **Talk it through with pharmacy.** If you have a specific reason for going above the maximum, a clinical pharmacist can review it with you. If they agree, the order can go in with that reasoning written down.\n3. **Pass along a reason.** If there's something I'm missing, tell me the clinical reason and I'll reconsider. I'd still recommend pharmacy review it before the patient gets the first dose.\n\nLet me know which you'd like."
      }
     ],
